## Repeated Tap Guard (Mandatory)

- **`AppButton`** / **`AppBadgedIconButton`**: enable repeated-tap guarding by default (`guardRepeatedTaps: true`) and bind disabled state (`onPressed: null`) while loading.
- Custom **`InkWell`**, **`GestureDetector`**, or **`IconButton`**: wrap callbacks with **`guardTap`** or an explicit in-flight guard.
- **State controllers:** auth, navigation, and destructive entrypoints must early-return when already loading or in a terminal completed state.
- **Listeners:** use **`listenWhen`** (or edge-triggered effect guards) for one-shot navigation so terminal states can never push duplicate routes.

---

## Dialogs & Bottom Sheets (Mandatory)

- Always use the project's shared dialog and sheet wrappers (`showAppDialog`, `showConfirmationDialog`, `showAppModalBottomSheet` + `AppBottomSheetBody` + `AppBottomSheetHandle`).
- Sheets: enforce consistent horizontal padding, unified icon leading glyphs, semantic danger color (`context.danger`) for destructive items, and bottom safe-area inset.
- **Forbidden:** bare `AlertDialog`, raw `showModalBottomSheet` missing bottom safe inset, or destructive/privacy actions firing without confirmation.

---

## Chrome-Preserving Errors (Mandatory)

When an initial list or detail fetch fails and **no** cached data is available:

- **Keep chrome visible** — preserve the app bar, back button, tabs, bottom navigation, and primary actions.
- Surface failures via **error toast** in a scoped listener — **never** replace the entire screen with a full-page error widget for tab or list loads.
- Render empty or retryable error states inside the **content area only**.
- Full-page error views are reserved strictly for standalone fatal/unrecoverable routes.

---

## System Insets & Keyboard (Mandatory)

Verify layouts on **both gesture navigation and 3-button navigation** — the lowest sheet row or input composer must never sit behind the OS navigation bar.

| Chrome | Bottom Inset Owner |
| --- | --- |
| `Scaffold.bottomNavigationBar` | Scaffold — body uses `SafeArea(bottom: false)` |
| Modal bottom sheets | Shared sheet body / `SafeArea(top: false)` once |
| Full-screen with keyboard | `resizeToAvoidBottomInset: true` + body `SafeArea` |
| Pinned composer + resize true | Composer uses `SafeArea(top: false)` + fixed padding — **no** extra `viewInsets.bottom` |
| Embedded composer + resize false | Add `viewInsets.bottom` (+ `paddingOf.bottom` only if outside `SafeArea`) |

- **Single keyboard mechanism:** never stack `resizeToAvoidBottomInset` + manual `viewInsets` + redundant `SafeArea` on the same composer without a documented reason.
- Never use hardcoded bottom pixel spacers that guess navigation bar height.
- Badged icons: use **`AppBadgedIconButton`** / **`AppBadgeOverlay`** with `IgnorePointer` on the badge so the full hit target remains clickable.

---

## End-User Copy Clarity

- Write strictly for **end users** — never surface raw pixel sizes, JPEG quality numbers, internal database column/RPC names, or cache keys in user-facing UI (unless inside admin/developer diagnostics).
- State clearly **what changes**, **where**, and any plan/tier impact in plain localized language.

---

## Tab Navigation & Active-Tab Re-Tap (Mandatory)

- **Preserve scroll on tab switch:** Switching between tabs must **never** reset scroll offset or trigger an automatic feed reload. Preserve scroll state via `PageStorageKey` / `AutomaticKeepAliveClientMixin` (or route/state preservation on web).
- **Re-tap active tab only:** Tapping the *already active* tab is the **only** tab tap that scrolls to the top and triggers a soft refresh.
- **Flutter `TabBar.onTap` trap:** In Flutter's `TabBar`, `_controller.animateTo(index)` updates `_tabController.index` *before* invoking `widget.onTap(index)`. Never check `if (index == 0 && _tabController.index == 0)` to detect a re-tap — it falsely evaluates to `true` on every switch to tab 0. Track the previously active tab index in dedicated state (e.g., `_currentActiveTabIndex`) to distinguish tab switching from active-tab re-taps.

---

## Zero-Count Engagement & Layout Reservation (Mandatory)

- **No phantom layout reservation:** When an entity/post has zero reactions, comments, and shares (or zero sub-items), render nothing — no empty summary rows, spacers, or dividers.

```dart
if (item.reactionsCount > 0 || item.commentsCount > 0 || item.sharesCount > 0) ...[
  EngagementStatsRow(...),
  const SizedBox(height: 8),
  const Divider(),
]
```

---

## Touch Targets

- Every interactive control must provide at least **44×44** logical pixels of tappable area (padding counts toward hit area).
